From da5cf372ae2855d8c78a6ef658eafb7a5c99e9d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:58:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc: security review and login watch (rwatch 3h); the
 front-chain watchdog names the rule

Security review, new and off by default (rwatch_review): every tick past the
boot grace inventories /jffs/scripts, /jffs/configs and authorized_keys by
hash, the other /jffs/.ssh files and /jffs/addons by size and date, every
cron entry that is not Reaper's own, and the exposure settings; diffs
against /jffs/reaper/review/baseline; writes /tmp/reaper/review.json; logs
once per change set. Advisory end to end - never FAIL or CRIT, no heal.
Login watch: a byte cursor on the system log (rotation-aware), ten or more
failed dropbear or httpd logins from one source inside one check become a
notice, logged once per source per hour. httpd: reaper_watch.cgi (status /
set / ack behind reaper_gate; ack writes the baseline with rjf_set and
re-runs the review detached); the no-report answer carries whether a
baseline exists so the pages show the pending state honestly. Firewall page:
the review card on the Status tab. Dashboard: the amber bar and the Security
Review posture row. Checked on metal (RT-BE96U, owner).

Front chain: a front-chain-drift now logs the offending rule text and the
fix (field, RT-BE88U with a Tailscale script at FORWARD position 1); built-in
targets listed in /jffs/reaper/front_exempt are ignored and logged
(reaper_hook.c/.h). The loopback-DNS check retries once before declaring a
failure (the nightly dnsmasq restart shares its tick boundary).

web.c is one file and also carries: the Devices presence changes (rdev_*),
the Warden dnsallow list and the three rcfg rows, the Storage volume pin
(store_status / store_set, rdev_store_base). defaults.c: rwatch_review,
rwarden_dns, rwarden_dns_feeds, reaper_store_vid, reaper_store_vname.

